legalExplanation:
The **Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps Act, 2003, section 3(1)(f)** gives the Corps power to **arrest with or without a warrant, detain, investigate and institute legal proceedings** in the name of the Attorney-General of the Federation against a person reasonably suspected of an offence under the Act or involvement in:
- criminal activity;
- chemical poisoning, oil spillage, nuclear waste or poisoning;
- industrial espionage or fraud;
- activity aimed at frustrating a government programme or policy;
- riot, civil disorder, revolt, strike or religious unrest;
- vandalisation of power transmission lines, oil pipelines, NIPOST cables, water board pipes or equipment.

The same section gives the Corps power to enter and search premises and seize materials suspected of being used in vandalisation (s 3(1)(e)). Those powers are tied to the Corps' statutory mandate.
